stability implications of forecast accuracy\n\n## Notation Summary\n\n| Notation | Description | Python Variable |\n|:---------|:------------|:----------------|\n| $m$ | Number of hourly observations | `m` |\n| $x^{(i)}$ | Solar irradiance for hour $i$ (W/m^2) | `x_train[i]` |\n| $y^{(i)}$ | Energy output for hour $i$ (kWh) | `y_train[i]` |\n| $w$ | Conversion efficiency factor (slope) | `w` |\n| $b$ | Baseline system losses (intercept) | `b` |\n| $\\alpha$ | Learning rate | `alpha` |\n| $J(w,b)$ | Cost function (mean squared error) | `J_history` |"
